DOMAIN	STRATUM	VARIABLE
# Source-of-truth HDSTATS-PC manifest.  The build embeds this file as
# pops/hdstats-pc-schema.h, so fitting and projection never depend on docs at
# run time. Three-column rows are input slots; COMPONENT rows declare the
# global PC registry. At projection, all oriented loadings whose absolute
# value meets pc-min-loading (default 0.10) are reported as signed
# standardized feature contributions (VAL), alongside the original input
# feature values (RAW); there is no top-N cap.
# With HDSTATS pc-proj=, only PC scores and selected contributions are emitted
# by default. Use pc-all=T to also emit ordinary HDSTATS metrics; QC output
# remains independently controlled by qc= (default F).
# Component IDs use PC_<domain-code>_<within-domain-number>:
# AM=ambiguity, IN=instability/stability, TR=transitions, SA=sleep architecture,
# UL=ultradian, ON=overnight, W=wake, N1/N2/N3=stage, R=REM.
# Stage-domain numbering groups broad themes where practical: occupancy/abundance,
# then timing/trend, then shorter/blockwise structure, then longer-horizon structure.
# Descriptions remain authoritative; numbering is not a cross-domain equivalence.
# To print this registry and the final model's oriented feature loadings:
# luna --hdstats-pc-desc model=hdstats-pc-coda-ref1.txt min-loading=0.10 > description.tsv
# The FTR_LOADINGS column contains semicolon-delimited feature=oriented-loading
# pairs meeting min-loading (default 0.10).
# Each non-comment row is one PC input slot. U_PEAK is shown as a commented stdout
# source; each UVAR group retains U_MOD and uses two derived inputs in place of U_PEAK.
# U_MOD_COS = U_MOD * cos(U_PEAK); U_MOD_SIN = U_MOD * sin(U_PEAK) (U_PEAK in radians).
# Per-sample/EDF ultradian names are U_DEPTH, U_PHASE, U_PHASE_VALID, U_AMP,
# and U_AMP_RAW; they are not additional PC input slots. U_MAG is the night summary.
# Five-state directional BOUT_TRANS_DENS pairs involving N1 are excluded from
# the PC panel; ordinary TRANS_DENS pairs involving N1 remain included.
# Argmax-stage-conditioned P_N1/PS and P_N3/PS remain HDSTATS outputs but are
# excluded from the N1/N3 PC panels because they are often undefined.
